id: pm-web-f3xo
title: Provide efficient backwards item history paging in the host SDK
description: "The installed public HistoryCommandOptions contract exposes limit but no before/after cursor or reverse scan. History event paging exposes a forward since cursor only. This API therefore re-reads the required latest compact suffix for older browser pages and bounds its HTTP result, while deep-page read cost still grows. The same item-history query declaration was inspected on npm 2026.10.20 and 2026.10.28. Open upstream search for history cursor found no exact existing issue. Track a host-provided backwards history page contract and adoption once supported; do not broaden project reads. Related delivery: pm-web-lgg5."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[1]: sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-28T16:21:08.275Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T16:26:42.580Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T16:22:23.374Z",codex-agent,"Discovered while delivering pm-web-lgg5. Public declarations checked: sdk/query/history.d.ts HistoryCommandOptions has limit and projection/filter fields, without before/after/since pagination; sdk/mutation-events.d.ts ListMutationEventsOptions has forward since only. HTTP payload size is bounded today, while older-page suffix reads grow with depth. No upstream issue was filed under the current task rules."
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  README.md,project,Documented deep-page native suffix read cost
